@startuml
!include _theme.puml
title GatoPago V3 — Seguridad multichain sin atomicidad ficticia

actor "Persona / guardians" as person
participant "App o emergency client" as client COLOR_WEB
participant "Relayers independientes\nGatoPago opcional" as relay COLOR_LIVE
database "Manifest store\npayload público" as db COLOR_DATA
participant "Account V3\nBase" as base COLOR_EXTERNAL
participant "Account V3\nArbitrum" as arb COLOR_EXTERNAL
participant "Account V3\nAvalanche" as avax COLOR_EXTERNAL

person -> client : propone Security Manifest N+1
client -> client : prevHash + chain scope +\nspend/admin/recovery + timelock
person -> client : threshold firma manifest
client -> db : publica payload inmutable

alt Cambio planificado
  par prepare en cada instancia
    relay -> base : prepare(N+1)
    relay -> arb : prepare(N+1)
    relay -> avax : prepare(N+1)
  end
  alt todas confirman + finality
    par commit independiente
      relay -> base : commit(N+1)
      relay -> arb : commit(N+1)
      relay -> avax : commit(N+1)
    end
  else alguna chain no responde
    relay --> client : pending / needs_security_sync
    client -> client : bloquear flows App/Payments\nno afirmar atomicidad onchain
  end
else Emergencia por signer comprometido
  par broadcast freeze/recovery
    client -> base : freeze/scheduleRecovery
    client -> arb : freeze/scheduleRecovery
    client -> avax : freeze/scheduleRecovery
  end
  client -> client : mostrar resultado por chain
end

note over base,avax
  Cada chain mantiene su manifest anterior hasta aceptar el nuevo.
  Una chain caída conserva riesgo residual: ninguna UI puede
  revocar onchain de forma atómica entre redes independientes.
end note

note over person,relay
  Firebase/correo nunca bastan.
  El payload puede relayarse sin secreto GatoPago.
end note

@enduml
